{"severity":"error","file":"errors/let_question_last_2.march","start_line":5,"start_col":4,"end_line":5,"end_col":18,"message":"`let?` cannot be the last expression in a block.\nAdd a Result-producing expression after it — for example:\n\n    let? x = might_fail()\n    Ok(x + 1)","code":"let_question_last","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/let_question_last_2.march","start_line":8,"start_col":2,"end_line":10,"end_col":5,"message":"`main` performs IO but declares no grant. The program reaches `IO.Console`; a `main` with no capability parameter is granted nothing.\nhelp: declare the grant `main` actually needs —\n        fn main(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console)) : ()\nor grant everything with `fn main(cap : Cap(IO))`.\n`forge fix` can apply this.","code":"cap_grant","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":8,"start_col":9,"end_line":8,"end_col":11,"text":"(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console))"},"labels":[],"notes":[]}
